  "notes": "ふざける can be used both playfully and critically depending on context. The command form ふざけるな is a strong expression of anger or disbelief.\n\nREGISTER:\nCasual/informal language. The colloquial contraction ふざけんな is even more casual/rough.\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- ふざけるな: stop messing around (command)\n- ふざけんな/ふざけんなよ: rough/angry version\n- ふざけ{半分|はんぶん}: half-joking\n- ふざけた～: ridiculous/inappropriate (adjective use)\n\nASPECT (ている):\nふざけている indicates an ongoing state of joking or messing around.",
